@startuml
!include style.puml
title Bounded destructive undo history

state "Live records: C\nHistory (oldest to newest): A, B" as BeforeChange
state "Live records: D\nHistory (oldest to newest): A, B, C" as AfterChange
state "Live records: C\nHistory (oldest to newest): A, B" as AfterUndo
state "Live records: E\nHistory (oldest to newest): A, B, C" as AfterNewChange

BeforeChange --> AfterChange : successful normal change (C differs from D)\nsave D, append C, publish D
AfterChange --> AfterUndo : undo\nsave C, publish C, remove C
AfterUndo --> AfterNewChange : successful normal change (C differs from E)\nsave E, append C, publish E

note bottom of AfterChange
The newest snapshot is restored first.
Only changed records add a snapshot, after saving succeeds.
At the 100-snapshot limit, discard the oldest snapshot
before appending a new predecessor.
end note

note bottom of AfterUndo
No forward state D is retained.
Successful undo shows all students and closes any attendance report.
Failed saves leave records, filter, report, and history unchanged.
end note
@enduml
